1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Pope John XVII''' (Latin: Ioannes XVII; died 6 November 1003), born John Sicco, was the bishop of Rome and nominal ruler of the Papal States for about seven months in 1003. He was one of the popes chosen and ecl
2 CONC ipsed by the patrician John Crescentius.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sicco was the son of another John Sicco,[2] and was born in the region of Rome then referred to as [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/14_regions_of_Medieval_Rome Biveretica].[3] Before entering the priesthood, Sicco had been marr
2 CONC ied and had three sons who also entered holy orders: John, bishop of Praeneste; Peter, a deacon; and Andrew, a secundicerius. 
2 CONT - [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_John_XVII En], [https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papa_Giovanni_XVII It]
