2 CONT '''Napomena:''' 
2 CONT * Nije bio ista osoba [https://www.geni.com/people/Andrija-Sicco/6000000115668584966 '''Andrija Sicco'''], sin od [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-John-XVII/6000000184169690842 pape '''Ivana XVII'''].
2 CONT * Neki izvori navode da je navodno jedan od njegovih potomaka kao njegov sin bio također i [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] koji je bio osnivač i rodonačelnik zadarske patr
2 CONC icijske obitelji Madijevci (Madi), koji se prvi put spominje u Zadru od 930.- 940. godine. Prema Andrijinoj oporuci iz 918. godine [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] se nigdj
2 CONC e ne spominje kao njegov sin ili brat, niti kao nećak (što ne isključuje mogućnost da mu je [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] možda to bio,  da li po muškoj ili ženskoj lini
2 CONC ji, iako se [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] spominje za njegovog života u Zadru ([https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.''']
2 CONC  je tada imao otprilike 8-9 godina 918. (919.) godine u trenutku smrti [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-Andrija/6000000216904032844 '''priora Andrije''']), kao jedan od prvih zadarskih priora koji se spominje 986. godine priliko
2 CONC m obnove zadarskoga [https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benediktinski_samostan_sv._Kr%C5%A1evana_u_Zadru samostana sv. Krševana]. 
2 CONT * Andrija je vjerojatno uz svog brata đakona [https://www.geni.com/people/Petar-%C4%91akon/6000000216906568830 '''Petra'''] imao još jednog [https://www.geni.com/people/unknown/6000000216940086837 neimenovanog brata] (odnosno još 
2 CONC braće i sestara) no njihova imena nisu zabilježena (niti su nam poznata), možda je [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] bio upravo sin odnosno potomak nekoga od njih, pa bi pre
2 CONC ma tome [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] bio možda Andrijin nećak (?), no kako nam nisu poznata imena roditelja od [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/600
2 CONC 0000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] kao i njegovo daljnje unatrag porijeklo, ne može se sa sigurnošću potvrditi točan obiteljski odnos odnosno srodstvo, no neupitno je da je [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000
2 CONC 000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] bio Andrijin srodnik, bilo najvjerojatnije možda kao Andrijin nećak (?), a ne kao Andrijin sin, odnosno potomak  od Andrijine braće (ili sestara), što je logično s obzirom da je [https://www.geni.c
2 CONC om/people/prior-Andrija/6000000216904032844 '''prior Andrija'''] 918. (919.) godine bio vrlo star i umro od bolesti, dok je [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.''']  u to vrijeme t
2 CONC ek bio maloljetno dijete. Možda je [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-Andrija/6000000216904032844 '''Andrija'''] bio skrbnik od [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madije I.'''] (ili ga je 
2 CONC Andrija možda posvojio ?), no o tome nema nikakvih tragova, zapisa i informacija koje bi to mogle potvrditi, tako da to može biti jedino samo predmet '''pretpostavke''', no ne točna činjenica o tome. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' 
2 CONT * He wasn't the same person  [https://www.geni.com/people/Andrija-Sicco/6000000115668584966 '''Andrew Sicco'''], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-John-XVII/6000000184169690842 '''Pope John XVII'''].
2 CONT * Some sources state that he was allegedly one of his descendants as his son, also of [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I'''], who was the founder and progenitor of the Zadar patri
2 CONC cian family Madijevci (Madi), which was first mentioned in Zadar from 930-940. According to Andrija's will from 918, [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I'''] is not mentioned anywhe
2 CONC re as his son or brother, nor as a nephew (which does not exclude the possibility that [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I'''] may have been his, whether through the male or female
2 CONC  line, although [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I'''] is mentioned during his life in Zadar (Madius I was approx. 8-9 years old in 918 (919) at the time of Andrew's death), as on
2 CONC e of the first priors of Zadar, who is mentioned in 986 during the renovation of the Zadar [https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benediktinski_samostan_sv._Kr%C5%A1evana_u_Zadru monastery of St. Chrysogonus].
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-Andrija/6000000216904032844 '''Andrew (Andrija)'''], in addition to his brother the deacon  [https://www.geni.com/people/Petar-%C4%91akon/6000000216906568830 '''Peter'''], probably had another 
2 CONC [https://www.geni.com/people/unknown/6000000216940086837 unnamed brother] (or more siblings: brothers and sisters), but their names are not recorded (nor are they known to us). Perhaps [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-
2 CONC Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I'''] was the son or descendant of one of them, and therefore [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I'''] might have been Andrew's nephew (?), bu
2 CONC t since we do not know the names of [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I''']'s parents or his further ancestry backward, the exact family relationship or kinship cannot be confirmed
2 CONC  with certainty, but it is unquestionable that [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I'''] was Andrew's relative, most likely as Andrew's nephew (?), or descendant of Andrew's brother(
2 CONC s) (or sisters), and not as Andrew's son, which is logical considering that the [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-Andrija/6000000216904032844 '''prior Andrew'''] was very old ( ) and died of illness in 918 (919), while [https://w
2 CONC ww.geni.com/people/prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I'''] was a minor child at that time. Perhaps [https://www.geni.com/people/prior-Andrija/6000000216904032844 '''Andrew'''] was [https://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC prior-prokonzul-Madije-I/6000000216813545821 '''Madius I''']'s tutor (caretutor) (or perhaps Andrew was adopted him ?), but there are no exists traces, records, or information that could confirm this, so it can only be a matter of
2 CONC  '''assumptions''', not an exact fact about that.
2 CONT __________________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ANDRIJA''', zadarski prior, živio je krajem IX i početkom X st. Kao uspješan trgovac stekao je velik imetak, kojim je slobodno raspolagao i na temelju kojeg je pripadao patricijatu. Njegova oporuka iz 918. dragocjen je dokument
2 CONC  za hrvatsku gospodarsku i kulturnu povijest jer pokazuje strukturu bogatstva patricija i upućuje na razmjere zadarske kopnene i pomorske trgovine. Djeci iz dvaju brakova te supruzi oporučno je ostavio 5 kuća, vinograde i zemlju, 
2 CONC 600 glava stoke sitnog zuba s pastirima i stoku krupnog zuba. Napose se, po srednjovjekovnom običaju, sjetio samostana, crkava i duhovnih osoba. Samostanu Sv. Krševana ostavio je vinograd, zemlju, roba, robinju, 100 glava sitne st
2 CONC oke, svileno ruho. Crkvi Sv. Petra poklonio je svilenu tkaninu a Sv. Tome ubrus te crkvi Sv. Anastazije srebrni vrč i svilenu tkaninu. Zadarskom biskupu Forminu ostavio je konja; đakonu Petru, svom bratu, srebrni vrč i srebrno sed
2 CONC lo itd. Za spas svoje duše namijenio je svećenicima 100 glava stoke sitnog zuba, 100 modija žita i bačvu vina; u istu svrhu dao je preostale ovce i koze, odredio da se proda brod u luci i oslobodi rob Marun sa ženom, kojemu je pok
2 CONC lonio vinograd. Za otkup zarobljenika ostavio je 100 solida.
2 CONT
2 CONT LIT.: Jaroslav Šidak: Historijska čitanka za hrvatsku povijest, 1. Zagreb 1952, 14–16. — Marko Kostrenčić, Jakov Stipišić i Miljen Šamšalović: Diplomatički zbornik, 1. Zagreb 1967. — Nada Klaić i Ivo Petricioli: Zadar u srednjem v
2 CONC ijeku do 1409. Zadar 1976, 82–83.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dva puta se ženio, i imao djecu iz oba dva braka. 
