2 CONT 2.         daughter .  The Chronicle of Joannes Archidiaconus Goricensis records that "sancto Stephano" betrothed "Emerici ducis Sclavoniæ" to "filia Cresimiri" but that the future bridegroom died the following year[129].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' ([1030]) to IMRE of Hungary, son of ISTVÁN I King of Hungary & his wife Gisela of Bavaria ([1007]-killed Bihar 2 Nov 1031).  
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Emeric_of_Hungary
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Emeric of Hungary Prince St. Imre, also Henricus, Emeric, Emerick, Emmerich, Emericus or Americus ... married a lady from among the following four/or five/ persons ('''''The indentity of his wife is disputed.''''' : 
2 CONT *Some say it was ''Irene Monomachina'', a relative of Byzantine emperor Constantine IX Monomachos, 
2 CONT *or ''a female member of the Argyros family'' to which Byzantine emperor Romanos III Argyros belonged. 
2 CONT *Other say it was''' Patricissa of Croatia''', the daughter of Krešimir III of Croatia. 
2 CONT *Another possible person may have been ''Adelaide/Rixa of Poland'' or ''one of her unnamed sisters''.
