2 CONT 2.       '''  HICELA Orseolo''' .  The Chronicon Venetum names "Hicelam" as eldest of the four daughters of "Petrus dux", naming her husband "Stefano Sclavorum regis filio"[97].  A charter dated Jul 1079 records a judgment against
2 CONC  the abbey of Cluny and in favour of the monastery of SS. Trinità e S. Michele di Brondolo relating to property at Fogolana, and recalls sales of property by "Anna comitissa relicta domini Vidonis comitis" to "Petrum ducem Venetia
2 CONC rum filium bonum [memorie] Petrus dux" and by "Vitalis et Aichelda filii boni [memorie] Petr ducis" to "fratrum eorum Petrum ducem Venetiarum"[98].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( after [1000] ) STJEPAN of Croatia, son of SVETOSLAV King of Croatia.  After his father recognised Venetian overlordship over Dalmatia [1000], Stjepan was sent as a hostage to Venice, where he married the Doge's daughter[
2 CONC 99].  After the fall from power of the Orseolo family in 1024, Stjepan left Venice to find refuge in Hungary which granted him Slavonia as an appanage[100].    
