2 CONT '''Petar Kanavelić''' ('''Kanavelović, Kanaveli, Canaveli, Canavelli, De Canavellis'''), poet and dramatist (Korcula, 27 December. 1637 - Korcula, January 16, 1719). In Korcula attended clerical school, 1655th inducted into the Gr
2 CONC and Chamber, 1660 -61. a municipal teacher. From 1663rd Chancellor of Korcula Bishop F. Manole, who was accompanied on his way to Rome 1663-64. and helped him in disputes with the island's population and canons. In Korcula in 1664
2 CONC . chosen for defense, then in Zadar Chancellor Venetian general governor of Dalmatia, C. Cornaro 1665-67. and A. Priuli in 1667-68. After returning to Korcula performed judicial duties, a clerk in the warehouse of grain, lawyer, m
2 CONC ember of the Small Council and envoy Korčulan commune in Venice 1673rd He also became involved in trade, oversaw the family estates on the island of Korcula, near Split and Trogir, was the owner of the shipyard in his hometown. He
2 CONC  maintained a connection with the Dubrovnik authorities, especially with Trstenička captains (Orebic), which is visited by sending them information on the whereabouts of the Venetian fleet. He sent the report to the Venetian autho
2 CONC rities of the Republic of Dubrovnik. He actively participated in Dubrovnik literary and theatrical life and was a member of the Academy empty. After probably the last time in Dubrovnik 1708th retired in Korcula. - His extensive wo
2 CONC rk of fiction form songs and dramas. He wrote occasional, začinke, začinke Pirna and love, satirical, and the religious epic. Probably not answer 1660th when to order, on the occasion of the arrival of the general governor A. Corn
2 CONC aro in Korcula, appointed two elogija and sang two couplet (not preserved), for which he received a fee, one of the first in Croatian literature. And the rest of his occasional deal with current events, and they have a certain amo
2 CONC unt documentary views of events and descriptions. Tom belongs to the genre of his first published and preserved song, repay essay about Dubrovnik earthquake in 1667. Town Dubrovnik nobility in cherry, lyrically finest collection o
2 CONC f songs Bunić N. and B. Bettera (Ancona 1667). Occasional five stanzas of Peter Zrinski from 1671 (Come on, come on love loved by, first published in the Construction of History of Croatian Literature, 1962, 28) in, for poets char
2 CONC acteristic, octosyllabic quatrains, the fictional monologue on the scaffold implicitly approved the execution Zrinski. That year, sent congratulatory pohvalbenu A. Zmajević the occasion of his appointment as Archbishop of Bar (Pri
2 CONC svijetlomu, pripoštovanomu Mr. Andrew Zmajević the episode when dedicated to the Archbishop of Bar). Squad with occasional conventional Baroque rhetoric and phraseology sang and apotheosis of Perast which fosters »flower noble her
2 CONC oism." Liberation from the Ottoman siege of Vienna 1683rd was the reason the two songs with panegiričkim intonation (song in praise privedroga John Sobieski, king poljačkoga, obranitelja Vienna, published in 1850, writing of II. e
2 CONC ulogizing the same King John Sobieski, published in the journal Slovinac, 1880, 18). He gave them the Polish king, who thanked him 1687th These songs are not distinguished by its special aesthetic level, but the show, especially t
2 CONC he first, some epic features. Inspired by the liberation of Vienna and go in Italian, which is trying to persuade the painter B. Staya to visually display this military success (Invito ad amico di Ragusa in pittore pinger un quadr
2 CONC o). 
2 CONT
