1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Nikola Spanić''' (Latinized as Nicolaus Spanich; 1633–1707) was a Roman Catholic prelate and nobleman of Korčula (an island in modern Croatia). A descendant of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spani_family Alb
2 CONC anian Spani family] of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drisht Drivasto], he served as the island's bishop from 1673 to 1707. After an earthquake in 1667 he restored a church dedicated to St. Anthony near the main town of the island
2 CONC .[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikola_Spani%C4%87 En]
2 CONT * https://www.catholic-hierarchy.org/bishop/bspanich.html
