1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MKV 5 - https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L99X-VQB1?mode=g&i=124&wc=9R2H-W3J%3A391644801%2C392240201%2C392245701&cc=2040054
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.3.1/TH-1971-28338-4469-12?cc=2040054&wc=MC5D-QTG:391644801,392240201,392245701
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Francis Stephen Lucic was a shipowner and a shipbuilder on the Island of Hvar, Dalmatia, Croatia. He spent his entire youth on the island, but shortly after his marriage he and his bride Joanna left his native town of Hvar
2 CONC  and went to the historic and picturesque capitol of the Province of Dalmatia, Split. Here on September 9, 1855, a son, Anthony Francis, was born to them, who eventually was to come to the wastelands of Texas and gain internationa
2 CONC l recognition for his famous Spindletop discovery of oil, and the consequent revolution of industrial America.
2 CONT * http://www.croatia.org/crown/croatians/www.croatians.com/OIL-LUCICH%20(ETEROVICH).htm
