1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Omiš doctor Dr. Jakov Mirkovic, apparently a "temporary Omisan", found himself in the city performing the service of a contracted municipal doctor. This lucid and well-educated physiocrat proposed to the Venetian 
2 CONC authorities the opening of a medical school in Dalmatia. He was a native of Hvar, and his family derived a lineage from the noble Mirković of Pag, and his name is therefore entered in the Pag book of nobles.
