1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anastasia was the daughter of Domenico Coschich and Tomasina Angelini. Marriage records are missing for Vrboska, but she wed Antonio Bruttapelle of Bassano del Grappa, Italy, sometime before her son's birth in 1791
2 CONC . The couple had at least three children, Giacomo (1791), Tomasina (1795), and Maddalena (~1797).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Coschich alias was Brescovich. The title "Pron" (with a tilde over the "ron") was used with the Coschich family name in Vrboska parish records, which may have meant "Paron" (landowner). Anastasia and her parents were buried at
2 CONC  the Chiesa B. V. Maria, aka Chiesa della Madonna, which is where the family was also buried. Anastasia's maternal grandfather was of a noble family in Hvar, Gabriel Angelini.
