0 @N6000000002187699070@ NOTE Emeric of Hungary (saint)
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT (Redirected from Imre of Hungary)
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Note: There was also a king of Hungary named Imre (Emeric), who ruled from 1196 to 1204. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Saint EmericPrince St. Imre, also Henricus, Emeric, Emmerich, Emericus or Americus (Székesfehérvár, 1007 (1000?) – Veszprém, September 2, 1031) was the son of Stephen I of Hungary. He was educated by Bishop Gerhard (Gerard Sagredo
1 CONC ; Saint Gellert) from the age of 15 to 23. He was intended to be the next monarch of Hungary, his father wrote admonitions to prepare him for this task, but he died at a young age, at hunting, by a boar. For his pious life and pur
1 CONC ity, he was canonized in 1083.
1 CONT
1 CONT Amerigo Vespucci was named after the saint.
1 CONT
1 CONT   This biography of a member of a continental European royal house is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it. 
